@page "/repair-or-replace-roof"
@{
    ViewData["Lang"] = "en";
    ViewData["SeoEn"] = "/repair-or-replace-roof";
    ViewData["SeoEs"] = "/es/reparar-o-reemplazar-techo";
}
<main class="resource-site" lang="en">
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_SeoIntentHeader")
    <section class="resource-hero systems-hero">
        <div class="site-shell">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Repair or replace</p>
            <h1>Repair or Replace Your Roof in Charlotte, NC</h1>
            <p>A patch is honest when the rest of the system will hold. A replacement is honest when leaks keep returning, storm damage is widespread, or the roof is near the end of its life. Majestic inspects first. We do not sell a replacement to win a claim.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a class="button button-gold" href="/free-roof-inspection-charlotte-nc">Free inspection</a>
                <a class="button button-ghost" href="/roof-replacement-cost-charlotte-nc">Replacement cost</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="resource-body section" id="process">
        <div class="site-shell resource-sections">
            <article><span>01</span><div>
                <h2>When a repair is the right next step</h2>
                <p>Isolated leaks, a few missing shingles, chimney flashing or a pipe boot can often be repaired if surrounding slopes are sound. See <a class="official-link" href="/roof-repair-charlotte-nc">roof repair in Charlotte</a> and the leak, wind and chimney guides.</p>
            </div></article>
            <article><span>02</span><div>
                <h2>When replacement is the smaller risk</h2>
                <p>Repeated leaks, sagging, widespread hail or wind, failed patches or a roof at the end of its life usually need a system replacement. Pair this with <a class="official-link" href="/roof-replacement-charlotte-nc">replacement</a> and <a class="official-link" href="/roof-installation-charlotte-nc">installation</a>.</p>
            </div></article>
            <article><span>03</span><div>
                <h2>Storms do not automatically mean a new roof</h2>
                <p>Visible storm patterns are documented as facts. The carrier decides coverage. Construction still has to match the roof that is actually there. Read the <a class="official-link" href="/storm-damage-roof-repair-charlotte-nc">storm hub</a> and <a class="official-link" href="/faqs">FAQs</a>.</p>
            </div></article>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="faq-section section" id="faq">
        <div class="site-shell faq-layout">
            <div><p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p><h2>Repair vs replace</h2></div>
            <div class="faq-list">
                <details><summary>Can you tell from the street?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. Pitch, decking, flashing and interior stains have to be inspected. A photo from the curb is a start, not a scope.</p></details>
                <details><summary>If insurance pays, do I have to replace?<span>+</span></summary><p>Coverage is the carrier’s decision. What the roof needs is a construction question. Those can differ. Majestic writes the construction scope; we do not waive deductibles or guarantee payment.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Can I replace only one slope?<span>+</span></summary><p>Sometimes. Matching color and remaining life still matter. We explain when a partial replacement is honest and when it creates a future leak line.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Does a storm automatically mean a new roof?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. Visible storm patterns are documented as facts. The carrier decides coverage. Construction still has to match the roof that is actually there.</p></details>
                <details><summary>Will a Tune-Up avoid replacement?<span>+</span></summary><p>The Tune-Up is maintenance on accessible areas. It is not a leak repair and not a replacement for a roof at the end of its life. See the <a href="/roof-tune-up-charlotte-nc">$350 Roof Tune-Up</a>.</p></details>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    @await Html.PartialAsync("_SeoIntentFooter")
</main>
